## Configuration

Settings come from environment variables only. See [docs/configuration.md](docs/configuration.md).

| Variable | Default | Meaning |
|---|---|---|
| `HOST` | `127.0.0.1` | Address to listen on (`0.0.0.0` in a container) |
| `PORT` | `8080` | Port to listen on (`0` picks a free one) |
| `LOG_LEVEL` | `info` | `debug`, `info`, `warn` or `error` |
| `SHUTDOWN_TIMEOUT` | `10s` | How long in-flight requests get after a stop signal |

## Development

Requires Go, make, a C compiler (for the race detector) and [golangci-lint](https://golangci-lint.run/).

| Command | What it does |
|---|---|
| `make build` | Build `bin/server` |
| `make serve` | Build and run the server in the foreground |
| `make test` | Unit and handler tests with the race detector |
| `make test-integration` | Run the built binary and test it over HTTP, including signal shutdown |
| `make lint` | golangci-lint |
| `make vuln` | govulncheck |
| `make coverage` | Race-enabled tests with a coverage floor |
| `make ci` | Everything CI runs |

See [docs/DEVELOPMENT.md](docs/DEVELOPMENT.md) for setup and scoped tests, and
[docs/http-api.md](docs/http-api.md) for the shipped HTTP contract.

